      "rows": [
        "4.1"
      ],
      "severity": "proof-gap",
      "finding": "The selected graph-spine generator is required only to have nontrivial image in the terminal neighborhood V. The subsequent assertion that its image in M is nontrivial/infinite does not follow: V\u2192M is not assumed \u03c01-injective, and a marked trace subsurface may have a kernel into its original F_j. Injectivity F_j\u2192M alone does not identify nontriviality in V with nontriviality in M.",
      "repair": "Choose the generator with nontrivial image in M directly. The original trace loop has infinite-order image in M; if every finite spine generator mapped trivially in M, that loop would too. A chosen nontrivial generator has nontrivial image in V and hence is essential on T. Original marked-surface injection plus the proved torsion-freeness then gives infinite order in M. No Statement change needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "AP2",
      "source": "research/inverse-problems-knot-theory-all-109-2026-10-19-owner-hyperbolization72-round1/generic-development/controlled-boundary/thm-closed-pl-boundary-homotopies-give-product-regions.md",
      "raw_sha256": "1baaba11c0f468cc25bc2ecad2f820d91ea1b6d1fa884c65dd5330ba3210f45b",
      "rows": [
        "3.1",
        "4.1",
        "5.1"
      ],
      "severity": "proof-gap",
      "finding": "The annular self-surgery supplier applies to an individual annulus with only regular two-sheeted self double curves. The product proof allows immersed intermediate annuli and arbitrary next undesired components without establishing this invariant. A pairwise cap swap can reassign sheets at an untouched triple value to repeated labels; later pairwise swaps before self cleanup can produce three preimages in one annulus. Its self-double locus then has intersecting preimage curves, so the disjoint two-preimage circle/arc cuts invoked in4.1 are not justified. The global (t,d) argument does not by itself supply these missing domains.",
      "repair": "State and prove an explicit priority invariant: before each surgery between distinct labels, every annulus is embedded. Immediately after that surgery, each output uses pieces from only two previously embedded annuli, each once, so it has at most two preimages of any value in itself. Clean all self double curves of those outputs before any next distinct-label surgery. Self cleanup does not reassign pieces to other labels and does not duplicate sheets, so this individual two-sheet bound persists; old triples have at most two copies of any label. Explain local third-sheet behavior and the decrease of the SAME global (t,d) during each cleanup. At restored embedded stages pairwise intersection curves have the required simple disjoint preimages. Fixed first boundaries, annulus topology and infinite-order core must remain explicit throughout. Alternatively provide a genuine multi-sheet surgery proof; do not just invoke the two-sheet supplier on a general immersed annulus."
    }
  ],
